From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:04:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 210/210] v4l2codecs: Add MPEG-4 Part 2, H.263 and Sorenson
 Spark decoders

Add v4l2slmpeg4dec, v4l2slh263dec and v4l2slsparkdec on top of
GstMpeg4Decoder, for devices with the MG4S, S263 and SPKS coded
formats.

The whole picture goes into one OUTPUT buffer with the VOL, VOP,
QUANTISATION and QUIRKS controls, or the H.263 PICTURE control. Drivers
which need the SLICE_PARAMS controls, the position of every video
packet or GOB, are refused: they are not filled. As there is no
per-picture array, there is no limit on the number of video packets or
GOBs of a picture.

The encoder deviations of the stream are passed as QUIRKS where the
driver can reproduce them, and the stream is refused where it cannot,
as the V4L2 Request hwaccel of FFmpeg does. Sprites and global motion
compensation, non-rectangular shapes, scalability and NEWPRED are
refused, as are H.263 B-pictures, PB-frames, reference picture
selection and resampling, which the controls do not describe.

The LOW_DELAY flag of the VOL is set while the stream has no B-VOP.

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
